cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this record, cite it and name the build you used. The built_on
  and integrity_sha256 rows of the meta table identify a build exactly, and
  ANCHORS.md ties each digest to a Bitcoin block.
type: dataset
title: "errata"
abstract: >-
  A public, verifiable record of one project's own corrections: every claim
  published and got wrong, what replaced it, which way the error ran, and who
  paid. Beside it, the full revision history of every published article, with
  the removed prose kept and each change labelled human, co-authored,
  assistant or automation. SQLite and plain SQL, sealed with a SHA-256 digest
  over every row and timestamped into Bitcoin with OpenTimestamps. The digest
  proves the contents are unchanged since the build. It does not prove any
  sentence in them is true.
authors:
  - name: "The Vera Project"
    website: "https://www.veraproject.xyz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeb2-spec/errata"
url: "https://www.veraproject.xyz/errata"
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
keywords:
  - corrections
  - errata
  - provenance
  - tamper-evident
  - opentimestamps
  - sqlite
  - human-ai-collaboration
  - ai-authorship-disclosure
  - open-data
